rings me to the third point by  flattening the sales funnel you're going  to close more deals and you close more  deals because you have the ability  through marketing automation to focus on  the right leads at the right time let me  give you a couple of examples and maybe  some of this has happened to you  the first scenario I downloaded a white  paper that was promoted on Twitter I  followed the link filled out the form  and downloaded the white paper but what  was interesting as I received a sales  call the same day and then I received  two more sales calls trying to close me  in two weeks now what's the problem with  that it was too much sales too much  pressure and all I did was download a  white paper they never even asked if I  got anything out of the white paper they  just treated me as a lead in the funnel  now let's look at the next scenario the  next scenario is I received an email and  it was a sponsored email from someone  that I already trusted and they pitched  a white paper well I went ahead and  downloaded that white paper and then  over the course of the next four months  I received invitations to download  additional white papers to attend  webinars helpful information about that  content and got a few emails that just  walked me along the process of what this  company can do and also highlighted some  success stories after those four months  I received a phone call it was  incredible  they knew the content that I had looked  at they knew which webinars  I attended and we had a good  conversation because it wasn't high  pressure they knew exactly the content I  was interested in and they were using  the phone call to gauge my urgency was I  ready to buy what was my time line and  so it was an intelligent conversation  about specific content what I found  valuable and really just gauging my  interest level see the result of that  type of scenario is that is going to  result in a high conversion qualified  sales call that has actionable results  marketing automation does require some  patience but it will limit the amount of  time you spend with leads that don't  exhibit any behavior of interest or  desire to become a customer and so  marketing automation enables you to  close the prospect more efficiently more  knowledgeably because you have a shared  experience shared content and you can  approach a phone call or a closing  conversation with specific information  about that prospect and you can use that  phone call simply to gather more data  rather than to apply pressure to make a  decision  a course of all these things happen  you're going to make more money but  you're going to make more money also by  evaluating your existing customers  through marketing automation you see  through marketing automation we can  nurture leads to become customers we can  nurture our existing customer base to  learn more information about them as we  learn where our customers live their  likes their dislikes their preferences  the content they find interesting the  products that they are more attracted to  then we can start conversing with them  on a more personable a more specific  level we can develop highly efficient  customer segments from the data that  we've accumulated and we could present  offers that are highly targeted relevant  and specific to each group of customers  the fifth reason why I absolutely love  marketing automation is that it helps me  identify my best customers I love going  through and looking for my top 20% of  customers and figuring out why are they  my top 20% and then I can build better  loyalty by giving better offers that are  more customized and personalized to them  and then I can develop an inner circle  mentality I can provide incentives I can  talk to them at a different level  because these are the ones that are most  likely going to be my advocates and so I  can feed them information I can treat  them differently because they're on a  different level than the rest of my  customers and a